# HOPE-V3 – COMPLETE LOCAL AI ENGINE MIGRATION
## Replace Existing On-Device AI / Gemma Runtime with Ollama-Compatible Local Model Architecture

### PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Upgrade the existing HOPE-V3 Android application by replacing the current on-device AI and Gemma-specific inference implementation with a completely local AI architecture.

The primary objective is to make HOPE's local intelligence work without internet connectivity.

IMPORTANT ARCHITECTURE DECISION:

Ollama is a model-serving and management runtime, not an AI model itself. The Android application must use an embedded llama.cpp runtime through Android NDK for direct on-device GGUF inference.

Implement an Ollama-compatible provider interface so the same AI service architecture can also connect to a local Ollama server on a computer when available.

Do not pretend that a remote computer's Ollama server is on-device inference.

