# PHASE 11 – OFFLINE / ONLINE MODE CONTROLLER

Create a dedicated AI mode selector.

Modes:

1. LOCAL OFFLINE.
2. LOCAL OLLAMA SERVER.
3. CLOUD AI.
4. HYBRID.

LOCAL OFFLINE:
- Android device runs the GGUF model.
- No internet needed for inference.
- Local memory and processing.

LOCAL OLLAMA SERVER:
- Connect to the user's own Ollama instance.
- Show server connectivity.
- Show available server models.
- Never label remote server inference as on-device inference.

CLOUD AI:
- Use existing Gemini integration when explicitly enabled.

HYBRID:
- Prefer local inference.
- Allow authorized cloud fallback only when explicitly configured.

When LOCAL OFFLINE is selected, absolutely prohibit cloud fallback.

Display the active provider on the conversation screen.

